WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:04.750
- All right so we are,

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.820
we're gonna to start in a few minutes.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.100
Probably a few seconds.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.050
- [Phillipe] You're online on Twitter,

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:17.050
should see the Twitter.

00:00:28.407 --> 00:00:29.363
- Should we start?

00:00:30.446 --> 00:00:32.150
- [Phillipe] Let's put this online.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.097
Okay then, go ahead, ready.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.310
- Hello, well, thanks
everyone for joining.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.550
The whole idea of this livestream

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.240
and we're thinking of doing
this as regularly as we can,

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:46.440
is obviously the world is going through

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.330
something of a crisis right now

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.487
around the COVID, coronavirus.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.850
And a part of that, obviously people are,

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:55.683
first and foremost,

00:00:55.683 --> 00:00:58.470
concerned about their and
the community's health

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.820
and the spread of the virus

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.680
and how to best stop that.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.460
But then, there's obviously
side-on effects of that

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:05.920
and one of them is that we're starting

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.480
to see increasing school closures.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:10.590
Obviously, other countries,
like South Korea, Japan,

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.190
and more recently Italy and France,

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:14.500
have closed down schools entirely.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.833
And we're starting to
see that in the US now.

00:01:17.833 --> 00:01:20.860
My children's school
was closed as of today.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:22.423
And obviously, Khan Academy,

00:01:23.274 --> 00:01:24.480
a non-profit mission of

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.700
free world-class education
for anyone, anywhere.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.930
The way that we've
tried to help doing that

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:31.270
is by creating resources online

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:33.300
that could be used in
conjunction with classrooms

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.490
that could also be used
independently by students.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.820
We think this is our duty
to really step up now

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:43.170
and make sure that as
many students as possible

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.470
feel supported as possible,

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.650
as many parents as
possible feel supported,

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:49.760
as many teachers as
possible feel supported.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:51.000
So, what we're gonna do today,

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.020
and this is all a little
bit of improvisation,

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.230
is I'll tell you what I've been telling.

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.212
We've been getting a lot of inquiries

00:01:57.212 --> 00:01:59.630
from various outlets and things.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.988
I'll tell you what we've
been telling everyone.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.760
What resources we're
gonna try to put together

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.010
and then, I'd just love to take questions

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:06.980
from anyone out there,

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:08.580
whether you're a parent, student, teacher,

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:09.770
or whether you're just someone

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.800
who's curious about things.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.020
So, big picture, what we're saying,

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:14.853
so first of all Khan Academy,

00:02:14.853 --> 00:02:16.720
many of y'all are familiar with it.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.370
We do have a lot of the core resources

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:21.810
that students of all ages would need

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.350
to be able to keep learning.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:26.620
If you start at the youngest age level,

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.320
we have Khan Academy Kids.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.180
Khan Academy Kids is for as
young as ages two to three,

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:32.980
but it will adapt the students all the way

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.190
to through the first grade standards.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:36.560
We've just added the
first grade standards,

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.840
and that's in reading, writing, math,

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.970
and social-emotional learning.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.140
We can talk about the
ideal use case for it,

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.790
I think for that younger crowd,

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:45.980
maybe 20 minutes a day

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:48.950
or at least no more
than 20 minute sessions.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.880
Ideally, sitting on the
lap or sitting next to

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.652
a parent or loved one who can

00:02:53.652 --> 00:02:55.130
work through it with them.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:57.930
But that could be an
interesting starting point

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:58.900
and we'll talk more about

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.050
some of the ways that you
could structure your day.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:04.480
As you get into early elementary,

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.910
mid-elementary, late-elementary
and even middle school,

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.990
on the English and Language Arts side,

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:11.980
we actually just launched,

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:12.970
it's actually not even launched,

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:15.110
it's a beta of our
English and Language Arts.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:17.280
It's not perfect, we have
to make some product changes

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.930
so that it can better work

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.260
for the English and
Language Arts modality.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.599
But it has some really
great content on it already.

00:03:23.599 --> 00:03:25.240
So, if you go to the Khan Academy,

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.720
the main dropdown menu on the top left.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.790
You'll see, when the menu comes down,

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:30.870
you'll see it on the bottom right,

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.717
it'll say ELA Beta,

00:03:32.717 --> 00:03:35.420
and then, you can pick the
appropriate grade level.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.810
Once again, I'll talk more
about how to use that,

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.640
but that has reading comprehension,

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.100
which is, I think, one of
the most important things

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:44.010
for parents and students
and teachers to keep up with

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:47.120
while we're going through
this unfortunate situation.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.640
On the math side,

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.010
this is probably what
we're most known for.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:52.470
A lot of people associate
us with those videos,

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:54.880
but actually I think the
most valuable thing we offer

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:57.950
is the ability for students to practice

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:58.860
as much as they need,

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:00.790
in any concept, all standards aligned,

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:02.070
at their own time and pace.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.640
That goes all the way from
the kindergarten standards.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:05.760
And, so do have an overlap

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.440
between Khan Academy Kids and the website,

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.267
where I would say if a student

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:13.210
is just learning to
read, still quite young,

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.270
Khan Academy Kids is a better resource.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:18.000
But if you're, for the
kindergarten, first-grade standards,

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.890
but if you have a second grader

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:22.441
who could use the remediation
or could use to go back,

00:04:22.441 --> 00:04:24.180
you've heard teachers
say they like to start

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.670
all their students back at kindergarten.

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:28.200
That actually could be
useful to just make sure

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.970
they have no Swiss cheese gaps.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.230
But for sure, once you get to
second, third, fourth grade,

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:35.949
all the way through middle
school, high school, and college,

00:04:35.949 --> 00:04:39.270
we've got you covered on
the math side of things.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:42.940
And then, as you go into a high school

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:44.600
science and social studies,

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:47.600
we have most of the core
subjects there as well.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:48.433
And then, on top of that we have

00:04:48.433 --> 00:04:50.380
the official SAT practice with this,

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.030
which is math, reading, and writing.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:54.760
I think that's appropriate
for any high school student

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.960
and even some precocious
middle school students,

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:59.140
if they wanna just make sure they

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.058
get that practice in those three areas.

00:05:01.058 --> 00:05:03.410
And for enrichment, I think
our computer programming

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.797
is really a lot of fun

00:05:04.797 --> 00:05:06.500
and it could be a really good way

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:10.109
to spend some down time
if students are at home.

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:11.580
The thing that I'm emphasizing

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.480
and we're emphasizing
as a team to parents,

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.170
is try to keep things--

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:19.630
Don't try to do everything all at once.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:20.860
It's not even healthy (laughs)

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:23.400
to be in front of a screen
for eight hours a day

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.290
while schools are closed.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:28.370
Try to focus first on just
the core fundamentals,

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:29.630
and then, if that's working,

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:31.240
then, layer on from there.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:33.370
In our minds, the core fundamentals are

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:36.540
the reading, the math, and the writing.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.850
The reading, you could use
our English and Language Arts

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:42.300
for students to get
practice reading passages,

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.070
answering comprehension questions on it.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.650
So, that's a good source
of reading practice.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:50.160
And also just reading books,
it's really that simple.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.700
We hope over the next week to send out

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.551
some reading lists and things
like that to make it easier

00:05:55.551 --> 00:05:58.630
for parents and teachers
and students on their own,

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:01.846
to know what types of
resources they can look at.

00:06:01.846 --> 00:06:04.410
On the math side,
depending on the age range,

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.780
and we're gonna send
out archetype schedules

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.630
over the next week.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:09.660
But for younger students,

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:11.350
I think sessions of about 20 minutes

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.720
is about appropriate.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.470
The important thing is
to just do the reading

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.220
and do the math every day.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.500
That's what really makes a difference.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.240
That will keep students from forgetting

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:21.250
over this time period.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:24.603
And, I believe actually can
help them, push them forward.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:27.930
And, if you can get that
reading and that math,

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:29.390
I would say, even two hours a day

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:33.000
is just the core base
for students of any age,

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:36.610
I think you're not going to be regressing

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:38.040
over this period

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.339
and might be progressing.

00:06:39.339 --> 00:06:40.830
And then, from there
you can layer on more,

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.200
especially for older students.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.487
And, I think once you get to middle school

00:06:43.487 --> 00:06:45.070
and high school students,

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:48.180
we can offer almost a full, complete day.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.810
And, we're also gonna send other resources

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:51.060
that are out there, podcasts,

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:53.793
other things you can read,
magazines that are good to read,

00:06:53.793 --> 00:06:55.810
in this obviously very interesting time

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.600
that our globe (chuckles) is facing.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:02.230
So, that's the initial thinking right now.

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:04.000
If you go to Khan Academy,

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.397
you'll see a little banner that says,

00:07:05.397 --> 00:07:07.000
"Hey, if you're seeing school closures

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.300
because of the virus, click here."

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:12.900
And, you'll see an evolving page

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:13.733
that has our resources,

00:07:13.733 --> 00:07:16.230
how do you get started, etc, etc.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:17.500
Some of what I just talked about,

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:20.240
we haven't put up yet so
please come on a daily basis,

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.040
it's going to be changing regularly.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.054
I'm hoping by Monday or Tuesday,

00:07:25.054 --> 00:07:26.890
we're going to put those schedules up.

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:30.660
So, if you are a student
or if you have a child

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:32.250
or if you're a teacher of children

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:34.470
who are of certain age groups,

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:36.410
what could a schedule look like for them,

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:37.630
including things like breaks.

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:39.870
Making sure everyone
gets time to run around

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:42.770
and play and explore and pay attention

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:44.340
to the news and all of that.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:47.830
But with that, I'd love to
take questions that folks have.

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:50.900
My colleague, Irene,
she's got a laptop here.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:52.200
- Hi, everyone.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.705
- We've got this light coming
through the blinds that's--

00:07:53.705 --> 00:07:54.538
- This light.

00:07:54.538 --> 00:07:56.513
It's been great to get
people's questions in.

00:07:56.513 --> 00:07:59.650
So, let me sound share some with you.

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:03.247
From Kristin Allen, we have a question of,

00:08:03.247 --> 00:08:05.740
"Is there a social-emotional learning

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:09.200
on Khan Academy for
first and second grade?"

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:10.690
- So, thanks for that question.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:11.930
So on Khan Academy Kids,

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:15.070
we do have social-emotional learning.

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:17.510
Social-emotional learning
is a very broad space,

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:18.580
but for Khan Academy Kids,

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:21.170
that is definitely
integrated into that offering

00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:23.100
and that's appropriate through students

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:25.000
up to six years old,

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.740
go through the six-year old standards.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:29.990
We don't have a deep
social-emotional learning

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:33.070
offering on Khan Academy Proper.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:34.530
I think that is a good call-out,

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:37.030
and as we ramp up materials,

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:38.550
I think it would be powerful for us

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:41.850
to think about how do we that, too

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:43.820
'cause a lot of what we've been building

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:45.340
over the many many years that are

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:46.940
I think going to be valuable

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:49.780
for people of this period.

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:51.540
We've been very focused
on your core academics.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.330
but I think what we're trying to do,

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:55.600
this live stream was really the first.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.230
Our first run at this,

00:08:57.230 --> 00:09:01.040
is try to give people
a sense of community,

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:02.620
try to give people a
sense of connectedness,

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:06.043
as we are all socially
isolating, so to speak.

00:09:06.043 --> 00:09:10.460
And, also give folks
materials and things to do.

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:13.460
So, you're gonna see all
of us at Khan Academy

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:15.730
broadening what we're talking about.

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:18.070
I think you're gonna,
as you see the schedules

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:19.920
and things that we put out next week,

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:20.753
we're gonna say,

00:09:20.753 --> 00:09:23.737
"This is your time to play."

00:09:23.737 --> 00:09:26.440
"This is your time to meditate maybe."

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:28.170
We're also gonna be exploring
with other partners,

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.910
ways that we can all
interact in deeper ways

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:33.480
so, that we don't all
feel completely isolated.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:35.302
And, also there is a lot of learning

00:09:35.302 --> 00:09:36.620
that's going on in the
broader world right now.

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:37.670
What's a virus?

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:38.770
How does it spread?

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:40.230
What's the proper response to it?

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:42.630
What's the economic
implications of all of this?

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:46.545
How are social interactions
going to change,

00:09:46.545 --> 00:09:49.400
maybe forever, after this?

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.600
So, there's a lot of real-life learning

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:54.091
that I think kids could, (laughs)

00:09:54.091 --> 00:09:55.290
and actually all of us,

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:57.530
could benefit of from in this period.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:59.250
- Yeah, there is a lot.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.710
But Kristin Allen, I just wanted to say

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:03.370
that her question was about

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:04.500
the first and second grades.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.267
Be sure to check out Khan Kids.

00:10:06.267 --> 00:10:08.010
You can download that app.

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:11.370
There are no ads in it,
no in-app purchases.

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:14.060
And, all the characters
really were designed

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:18.291
specifically to foster those tips

00:10:18.291 --> 00:10:19.758
We've got more questions coming in.

00:10:19.758 --> 00:10:21.280
- [Phillipe] One good thing to clarify,

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:22.880
on the Facebook page,

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.450
they see my name on there,

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:25.440
because it's originating,

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:27.750
it says Phillipe live. (laughs)

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.390
- Okay, Phillipe just told
us on the Facebook page,

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:32.290
you might be seeing, "Phillipe Live."

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:33.737
That's still us, it's fully--

00:10:33.737 --> 00:10:35.020
- [Phillipe] It's originating from

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:35.920
the video manager here. (laughs)

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:37.770
- Okay, yes, Phillipe is our video manager

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:38.690
and he's right on the other side

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:41.136
of the screen. (Phillipe chuckles)

00:10:41.136 --> 00:10:42.473
- We got a few more questions.

00:10:42.473 --> 00:10:43.460
